# Copy to web/.env.local. Nothing here is required to browse the public pages —
# the landing page, national overview, district lookup and method page all work
# with no configuration at all.

# --- Supabase (staff sign-in) ---------------------------------------------
# The same project the Streamlit app authenticates against. Accounts are
# provisioned by an administrator and their role/district scope is read from the
# `profiles` table (schema in ../supabase/schema.sql) — a signed-in user cannot
# choose a role. Without these, the staff portals render an access notice and
# the sign-in form explains that it is not configured.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Supabase (account management) ----------------------------------------
# Required only for the Administration -> Users & roles panel (create,
# edit, and deactivate staff accounts). This is the `service_role` key, not
# the anon key above -- it bypasses Row Level Security entirely, which is
# what lets it create an auth user and read every account for the admin
# table. It deliberately carries NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix: that prefix tells
# Next to inline a value into the JavaScript shipped to every visitor's
# browser, and this key must never be in that bundle. `src/lib/supabase/admin.ts`
# is the only file that reads it, and `import 'server-only'` there makes it a
# build error, not just a lint warning, if that ever changes.
#
# Get it from the same Supabase project: Settings -> Data API -> "service_role"
# "secret" key. Without this set, the admin panel's account table and forms
# render a clear "not configured" message rather than failing silently.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Rate limiting (production deployments) -------------------------------
# Sign-in and alert-subscription attempts are rate-limited (5 or 10 per
# window, by email and IP -- see src/lib/rate-limit.ts). Without these two
# set, the limiter falls back to counting in server memory, which is only
# correct for a single long-lived process (`next start`) -- on a serverless
# platform (Vercel included), every function instance gets its own empty
# counter, so the real limit becomes (this limit x however many instances
# happen to be warm). Add the Upstash integration from the Vercel Marketplace
# (or create a free database directly at upstash.com) and these two get set
# automatically; the limiter then checks one shared counter across every
# instance.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Account-creation email (optional) -------------------------------------
# When a national administrator creates a staff account or resets a password,
# the temporary credentials are emailed to the new account automatically if
# these are set -- see src/lib/email.ts. Without them, account creation still
# works exactly as before: the password is shown once in the admin panel for
# the administrator to copy and hand over out of band.
#
# These are separate from the same-named secrets the `refresh-data` GitHub
# Actions workflow uses -- that workflow runs entirely outside Vercel, so it
# needs its own copies as repo secrets; this app needs its own copies here as
# Vercel environment variables. Same resend.com account works for both.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Optional: defaults to DengueSentinel <onboarding@resend.dev>, whose sandbox
# restriction (see dengue.platform.alerts) only actually delivers to the
# Resend account's own verified address -- set this once a real sending
# domain is verified on Resend, so it can reach every new account for real.
ALERT_FROM_EMAIL=

# --- Development preview --------------------------------------------------
# Renders the staff portals under a chosen role WITHOUT signing in, so they can
# be reviewed on a checkout with no Supabase project. This is deliberately not
# the demo role switcher the Streamlit app removed: it is server-side, opt-in,
# and refuses to do anything when NODE_ENV=production.
#
# DENGUE_DEV_ROLE=moh_officer
# DENGUE_DEV_DISTRICTS=colombo,gampaha
